{"id":"punjab-paddy","name":"Kharif paddy belt, Punjab","region":"India","continent":"Asia","change_type":"crop","product":"GCOV","bbox":[75.6,30.2,76.3,30.75],"story":{"headline":"Watching a rice season breathe, field by field","what":"Paddies are flooded for transplanting (dark), the canopy grows (bright), then harvest and residue burning reset them. Only fields showing the full flood-then-growth signature are labelled rice; fields with a weaker swing fall under 'other active cropland', so the rice figure is a lower bound.","physics":"Flooded paddy = specular water, very dark. As rice tillers grow, volume scattering raises HV by 5-10 dB within weeks. The V-shaped HV curve is the radar fingerprint of rice. S-band responds more to leaves, L-band to stems and the soil-water interface.","drivers":"Monsoon-timed transplanting, groundwater irrigation, procurement-driven rice monoculture, Aug-Sep 2026 floods that destroyed standing crops.","caveats":"Rain on bare soil also brightens HH; use HV and the temporal shape, not single dates."},"s_band":true,"window":["2026-06-17","2026-11-10"],"bounds":[75.6,30.2,76.3,30.75],"center":[75.94999999999999,30.475],"demo":false,"band":"L","layers":{"frames":{"kind":"rgb","legend":{"type":"rgb","items":[{"label":"HH: surface & double bounce","color":"#e34948"},{"label":"HV: volume (vegetation)","color":"#1baf7a"},{"label":"HH/HV ratio","color":"#2a78d6"}]},"items":[{"date":"2026-06-28","url":"sites/punjab-paddy/frames/20260628.webp"},{"date":"2026-07-10","url":"sites/punjab-paddy/frames/20260710.webp"},{"date":"2026-07-10","url":"sites/punjab-paddy/frames/20260710.webp"},{"date":"2026-07-22","url":"sites/punjab-paddy/frames/20260722.webp"},{"date":"2026-08-15","url":"sites/punjab-paddy/frames/20260815.webp"},{"date":"2026-08-27","url":"sites/punjab-paddy/frames/20260827.webp"},{"date":"2026-09-08","url":"sites/punjab-paddy/frames/20260908.webp"},{"date":"2026-09-08","url":"sites/punjab-paddy/frames/20260908.webp"},{"date":"2026-09-20